<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SAfrica issues 26,250 T white maize export permits.</title>
<headline>SAfrica issues 26,250 T white maize export permits.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's Maize Board said on Wednesday it had issued export permits to private traders covering 26,250 tonnes of white maize for shipment in the months of February to end-April.</p>
<p>No permits for yellow maize had been issued.</p>
<p>This brings the total amount of maize exported by private players in the 1996/97 marketing year to over 1.68 million tonnes. In terms of the marketing scheme, traders may export a total of 1.8 million tonnes.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom 27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
